{"api_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/37762","collected_at":"2026-09-27T21:56:43.107598+00:00","comments":[{"author_association":"COLLABORATOR","body":"This is expected behavior; see https://github.com/jax-ml/jax/issues/37766#issuecomment-4482876732.","created_at":"2026-05-18T22:41:28Z","html_url":"https://github.com/jax-ml/jax/issues/37762#issuecomment-4482884283","id":4482884283,"issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/37762","minimized":null,"node_id":"IC_kwDOCTkjjc8AAAABCzNiuw","performed_via_github_app":null,"pin":null,"reactions":{"+1":0,"-1":0,"confused":0,"eyes":0,"heart":0,"hooray":0,"laugh":0,"rocket":0,"total_count":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/4482884283/reactions"},"updated_at":"2026-05-18T22:41:28Z","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/4482884283","user":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/781659?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jakevdp","id":781659,"login":"jakevdp","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc4MTY1OQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp","user_view_type":"public"}}],"issue":{"active_lock_reason":null,"assignee":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/781659?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jakevdp","id":781659,"login":"jakevdp","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc4MTY1OQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp","user_view_type":"public"},"assignees":[{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/781659?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jakevdp","id":781659,"login":"jakevdp","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc4MTY1OQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp","user_view_type":"public"}],"author_association":"NONE","body":"### Description\n\nJAX's CPU backend enables the processor's DAZ (Denormals-Are-Zero) flag, which causes all subnormal floating-point inputs to be silently treated as zero before any arithmetic. This produces qualitatively incorrect results across a range of mathematical functions — not just slightly inaccurate, but fundamentally wrong (finite values become ±inf, or small nonzero values become zero).\n\nThe issue affects both `float32` and `bfloat16`. It does **not** affect `float16`, which appears to take a different lowering path through XLA.\n\nAffected operations confirmed so far:\n\n| Op | Input | Expected | JAX returns |\n|----|-------|----------|-------------|\n| `jnp.log(x)` | subnormal | large negative finite | `-inf` |\n| `jnp.sqrt(x)` | subnormal | small positive | `0.0` |\n| `lax.rsqrt(x)` | subnormal | large positive finite | `+inf` |\n| `jnp.log1p(x)` | subnormal | ≈ x | `0.0` |\n| `lax.lgamma(x)` | subnormal | large positive | wrong value |\n\nThe failures are silent — no exception, no warning, just arithmetically incorrect output.\n\n## Reproducer\n\n```python\nimport warnings\nimport numpy as np\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nfrom jax import lax\n\ntiny = np.finfo(np.float32).tiny\n\nx = np.array([\n    np.nextafter(tiny, np.float32(0)),\n    np.float32(1e-40),\n    np.float32(1e-43),\n], dtype=np.float32)\n\nfor name, jfn, nfn in [\n    (\"log\",   jnp.log,   np.log),\n    (\"sqrt\",  jnp.sqrt,  np.sqrt),\n    (\"rsqrt\", lax.rsqrt, lambda a: np.float32(1) / np.sqrt(a)),\n    (\"log1p\", jnp.log1p, np.log1p),\n]:\n    with warnings.catch_warnings():\n        warnings.simplefilter(\"ignore\")\n        np_out  = nfn(x)\n        jax_out = np.asarray(jfn(jnp.array(x)))\n    print(f\"{name}:  numpy={np_out}  jax={jax_out}\")\n```\n\n## Expected output\n\n```\nlog:   numpy=[-87.33655  -92.10341  -99.01625]  jax=[-87.33655  -92.10341  -99.01625]\nsqrt:  numpy=[1.084202e-19 9.999973e-21 3.154238e-22]  jax=[1.084202e-19 9.999973e-21 3.154238e-22]\nrsqrt: numpy=[9.223373e+18 1.000003e+20 3.170338e+21]  jax=[9.223373e+18 1.000003e+20 3.170338e+21]\nlog1p: numpy=[1.175494e-38 9.999946e-41 9.949219e-44]  jax=[1.175494e-38 9.999946e-41 9.949219e-44]\n```\n\n## Actual output\n\n```\nlog:   numpy=[-87.33655  -92.10341  -99.01625]  jax=[-103.97208 -103.97208 -103.97208]\nsqrt:  numpy=[1.084202e-19 9.999973e-21 3.154238e-22]  jax=[0. 0. 0.]\nrsqrt: numpy=[9.223373e+18 1.000003e+20 3.170338e+21]  jax=[inf inf inf]\nlog1p: numpy=[1.175494e-38 9.999946e-41 9.949219e-44]  jax=[0. 0. 0.]\n```\n\n## Notes\n\n- Root cause: XLA sets the MXCSR DAZ bit on x86 CPUs, flushing subnormals to zero before ALU operations. This is a performance optimization in some HPC contexts but breaks IEEE 754 compliance.\n- The same `bfloat16` subnormal range overlaps with `float32` (both use 8 exponent bits), so bfloat16 is equally affected.\n- `float16` is not affected.\n- Normal inputs (values ≥ `np.finfo(np.float32).tiny`) compute correctly.\n- This has been observed consistently across multiple JAX versions on x86 CPU.\n\n### System info (python version, jaxlib version, accelerator, etc.)\n\n```\njax:     0.10.1.dev20260513+64f6e229b\njaxlib:  0.10.0\nnumpy:   2.4.4\nscipy:   1.17.1\npython:  3.12.3\nOS:      Linux-6.14.0-37-generic-x86_64-with-glibc2.39\nbackend: cpu\n```","closed_at":"2026-05-18T22:41:28Z","closed_by":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/781659?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jakevdp","id":781659,"login":"jakevdp","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc4MTY1OQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp","user_view_type":"public